SUMMARY:Power Nadeshiko Women's Empowerment Project community screening
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a free community screening and panel discussion to 
 learn practical knowledge that could one day help you\, your family\, your
  friends\, or someone in need. Together\, we can build a stronger and more
  compassionate community. The Power Nadeshiko Women's Empowerment Project 
 is a community-led initiative that empowers and educates culturally and li
 nguistically diverse communities to address gender-based and domestic and 
 family violence through multilingual educational resources and community e
 ngagement. Discussion topics include: mental health and domestic and famil
 y violence postnatal depression misogyny and gender-based discrimination t
 echnology-facilitated abuse coercive control laws children living with tra
 uma and intergenerational trauma elder abuse survivor stories. Program: 9.
 30am - Welcome and opening 9.55–10.45am - Community screening 10.45–11
 .35am - Panel discussion 11.35–11.45am - Feedback and project updates 11
 .45am–12.15pm - Networking and morning tea (complimentary). Venue: Garde
 n City Library\, Meeting Room. Address: Level R4\, Yellow Car Park\, Westf
 ield Mount Gravatt\, Cnr Logan Road & Kessels Rd\, Upper Mount Gravatt QLD
  4122. Free parking available. The project is proudly funded by the Queens
 land Government through the Empowering Multicultural Community Projects Gr
 ant.
